(High-feedrate positioning: emit one single-axis positioning move as either a)
(true rapid or a G1 at the high feed, per _pl_hf_x / _pl_hf_z.)
(CALL axis[1] target[2] restore_feed[3])
(axis 0 = X, the radial move; axis 1 = Z, the axial one.)

(WHY A SUBROUTINE AND NOT 13 INLINE CONDITIONALS. Every positioning move the)
(polyline emits is SINGLE-AXIS - measured, 148 rapids on testing_15_5 and not)
(one of them moves both X and Z - so which axis a site is belongs to the site)
(and the only question left is G0 or G1. Centralising it puts the FEED RESTORE)
(below in one place instead of thirteen.)

(THE FEED RESTORE IS THE WHOLE RISK. F is modal, so a G1 issued at the high)
(feed leaves it set, and the next cutting move that does not name its own F)
(would run at it. lathe_level_pass has such a path: with the profile-angle)
(approach off, the level cut takes the F last set. So every converted move)
(puts the caller's feed back before returning, and the caller passes the feed)
(that should be in effect afterwards.)
o<hf_move> sub
	#<hf_axis>    = #1
	#<hf_target>  = #2
	#<hf_restore> = #3

	#<hf_g1> = 0
	o<hf_pick> if [#<hf_axis> LT 0.5]
		#<hf_g1> = #<_pl_hf_x>
	o<hf_pick> else
		#<hf_g1> = #<_pl_hf_z>
	o<hf_pick> endif

	(a high feed of 0 means the operator asked for the mode but gave no rate -)
	(posting G1 F0 would stop the machine dead, so fall back to a true rapid)
	o<hf_rate> if [#<_pl_hf_feed> LE 0.0001]
		#<hf_g1> = 0
	o<hf_rate> endif

	o<hf_do> if [#<hf_g1> GT 0]
		o<hf_ax1> if [#<hf_axis> LT 0.5]
			G1 F#<_pl_hf_feed> X#<hf_target>
		o<hf_ax1> else
			G1 F#<_pl_hf_feed> Z#<hf_target>
		o<hf_ax1> endif
		o<hf_rst> if [#<hf_restore> GT 0.0001]
			F#<hf_restore>
		o<hf_rst> endif
	o<hf_do> else
		o<hf_ax0> if [#<hf_axis> LT 0.5]
			G0 X#<hf_target>
		o<hf_ax0> else
			G0 Z#<hf_target>
		o<hf_ax0> endif
	o<hf_do> endif
o<hf_move> endsub
